concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7(3) Constitution of Commission"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-7-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Before the Governor-General appoints a person as a member of the Commission or as Chairperson, the Minister must:  (a) be satisfied that the person qualifies for the appointment because of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in, industry, commerce, economics, law, public administration or consumer protection; and  (b) consider whether the person has knowledge of, or experience in, small business matters; and  (c) if there is at least one fully-participating jurisdiction—be satisfied that a majority of such jurisdictions support the appointment." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Before the Governor-General appoints a person as a member of the Commission or as Chairperson, the Minister must:  (a) be satisfied that the person qualifies for the appointment because of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in, industry, commerce, economics, law, public administration or consumer protection; and  (b) consider whether the person has knowledge of, or experience in, small business matters; and  (c) if there is at least one fully-participating jurisdiction—be satisfied that a majority of such jurisdictions support the appointment."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d34c01800ce86c6ae93f2bb8d7f41b4600d322fec2f75068fe18dc33899d31c3" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7 ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Minister must be satisfied that the person qualifies for appointment." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
