doc:sec-7-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "7(3) Constitution of Commission" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Before the Governor-General appoints a person as a member of the Commission or as Chairperson, the Minister must:  (a) be satisfied that the person qualifies for the appointment because of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in, industry, commerce, economics, law, public administration or consumer protection; and  (b) consider whether the person has knowledge of, or experience in, small business matters; and  (c) if there is at least one fully-participating jurisdiction—be satisfied that a majority of such jurisdictions support the appointment." ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7(4) Constitution of Commission"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-7-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) At least one of the members of the Commission must be a person who has knowledge of, or experience in, consumer protection. Note: Under section 23 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013, the Chairperson may enter into contracts and other arrangements on behalf of the Commonwealth." ;
    skos:definition "(4) At least one of the members of the Commission must be a person who has knowledge of, or experience in, consumer protection. Note: Under section 23 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013, the Chairperson may enter into contracts and other arrangements on behalf of the Commonwealth."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c4f0845d3965e3327d88b225238c109aa84f4664633c53dadf3c079f056b0804" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-7 ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Member of Commission must have knowledge or experience in consumer protection." ;
