concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-25 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "25 Delegation by Commission"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-25 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate to a member of the Commission, either generally or otherwise as provided by the instrument of delegation, any of its powers under this Act (other than Part VIIA or section 152ELA), a gas market instrument, the consumer data rules, Procedural Rules under Part XIC, the Telecommunications Act 1997, the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999, the Water Act 2007, Rules of Conduct under Part 20 of the Telecommunications Act 1997, the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011, regulations under the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011, or the Australian Postal Corporation Act 1989, other than this power of delegation and its powers to grant, revoke or vary an authorisation. Note: Section 95ZD allows the Commission to delegate certain powers under Part VIIA to a member of the Commission.  (2) A power so delegated may be exercised or performed by the delegate in accordance with the instrument of delegation.  (3) A delegation under this section is revocable at will and does not prevent the exercise of a power by the Commission." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate to a member of the Commission, either generally or otherwise as provided by the instrument of delegation, any of its powers under this Act (other than Part VIIA or section 152ELA), a gas market instrument, the consumer data rules, Procedural Rules under Part XIC, the Telecommunications Act 1997, the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999, the Water Act 2007, Rules of Conduct under Part 20 of the Telecommunications Act 1997, the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011, regulations under the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011, or the Australian Postal Corporation Act 1989, other than this power of delegation and its powers to grant, revoke or vary an authorisation. Note: Section 95ZD allows the Commission to delegate certain powers under Part VIIA to a member of the Commission.  (2) A power so delegated may be exercised or performed by the delegate in accordance with the instrument of delegation.  (3) A delegation under this section is revocable at will and does not prevent the exercise of a power by the Commission."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6ca8621bf4ebac3a3ace41c892688d9186dbbd9e697dbf132e0442ce868f6231" ;
    cof:pageNumber "87"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-25-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-25-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-25-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.87" .
doc:sec-25 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "25 Delegation by Commission" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate to a member of the Commission, either generally or otherwise as provided by the instrument of delegation, any of its powers under this Act (other than Part VIIA or section 152ELA), a gas market instrument, the consumer data rules, Procedural Rules under Part XIC, the Telecommunications Act 1997, the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999, the Water Act 2007, Rules of Conduct under Part 20 of the Telecommunications Act 1997, the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011, regulations under the National Broadband Network Companies Act 2011, or the Australian Postal Corporation Act 1989, other than this power of delegation and its powers to grant, revoke or vary an authorisation. Note: Section 95ZD allows the Commission to delegate certain powers under Part VIIA to a member of the Commission.  (2) A power so delegated may be exercised or performed by the delegate in accordance with the instrument of delegation.  (3) A delegation under this section is revocable at will and does not prevent the exercise of a power by the Commission." ;
    cof:pageNumber "87"^^xsd:integer .

