concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29BA Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-29ba ;
    values:originalText "Council  (1) A State/Territory energy law may confer functions or powers, or impose duties, on the Council for the purposes of that law. Note: Section 29BC sets out when such a law imposes a duty on the Council.  (2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or power, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law to the extent to which:  (a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would contravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties that may be imposed on the Council; or  (b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative power of the Commonwealth.  (3) The Council cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a power, under a State/Territory energy law unless the conferral of the function or power, or the imposition of the duty, is in  Chapter 1  Preliminary" ;
    skos:definition "Council  (1) A State/Territory energy law may confer functions or powers, or impose duties, on the Council for the purposes of that law. Note: Section 29BC sets out when such a law imposes a duty on the Council.  (2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or power, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law to the extent to which:  (a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would contravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties that may be imposed on the Council; or  (b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative power of the Commonwealth.  (3) The Council cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a power, under a State/Territory energy law unless the conferral of the function or power, or the imposition of the duty, is in  Chapter 1  Preliminary"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "15b42c09c8a6f64f15078c22ffb69551a48af5540c460d66a8c18851cea82033" ;
    cof:pageNumber "93"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29ba-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.93" .
doc:sec-29ba a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "29BA Commonwealth consent to conferral of functions etc. on" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Council  (1) A State/Territory energy law may confer functions or powers, or impose duties, on the Council for the purposes of that law. Note: Section 29BC sets out when such a law imposes a duty on the Council.  (2) Subsection (1) does not authorise the conferral of a function or power, or the imposition of a duty, by a State/Territory energy law to the extent to which:  (a) the conferral or imposition, or the authorisation, would contravene any constitutional doctrines restricting the duties that may be imposed on the Council; or  (b) the authorisation would otherwise exceed the legislative power of the Commonwealth.  (3) The Council cannot perform a duty or function, or exercise a power, under a State/Territory energy law unless the conferral of the function or power, or the imposition of the duty, is in  Chapter 1  Preliminary" ;
    cof:pageNumber "93"^^xsd:integer .

