    cof:title "29BB(2) How duty is imposed" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The duty is taken not to be imposed by this Part (or any other law of the Commonwealth) to the extent to which:  (a) imposing the duty is within the legislative powers of the State or Territory concerned; and  (b) imposing the duty by the law of the State or Territory is consistent with the constitutional doctrines restricting the duties that may be imposed on the Council. Note: If this subsection applies, the duty will be taken to be imposed by force of the law of the State or Territory (the Commonwealth having consented under section 29BA to the imposition of the duty by that law). Commonwealth legislative power sufficient to support duty but State or Territory legislative powers are not" ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29BB(3) How duty is imposed"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-29bb-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If, to ensure the validity of the purported imposition of the duty, it is necessary that the duty be imposed by a law of the Commonwealth (rather than by the law of the State or Territory), the duty is taken to be imposed by this Part to the extent necessary to ensure that validity." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If, to ensure the validity of the purported imposition of the duty, it is necessary that the duty be imposed by a law of the Commonwealth (rather than by the law of the State or Territory), the duty is taken to be imposed by this Part to the extent necessary to ensure that validity."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8324be5b51fdcc596e42487a4b1d83397f4c87d8a1db7155b53fe8884e4f530a" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Duty imposed by law of the Commonwealth if necessary for validity" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
