concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29BB(4) How duty is imposed"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-29bb-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If, because of subsection (3), this Part is taken to impose the duty, it is the intention of the Parliament to rely on all powers available to it under the Constitution to support the imposition of the duty by this Part.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 The National Competition Council  Part IIA  Section 29BC  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If, because of subsection (3), this Part is taken to impose the duty, it is the intention of the Parliament to rely on all powers available to it under the Constitution to support the imposition of the duty by this Part.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 The National Competition Council  Part IIA  Section 29BC  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a4b877cf76bf56b21dc5fa652a3e5015151103b6cbd6a7c6335b490a9e97f1a6" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29bb ;
