concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29C Membership of Council"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-29c ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Council consists of the Council President and up to 4 other Councillors.  (2) Each Councillor is to be appointed by the Governor-General, for a term of up to 5 years.  (3) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as a Councillor or Council President unless the Governor-General is satisfied that:  (a) the person qualifies for the appointment because of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in, industry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or public administration; and  (b) a majority of the States and Territories that are parties to the Competition Principles Agreement support the appointment." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Council consists of the Council President and up to 4 other Councillors.  (2) Each Councillor is to be appointed by the Governor-General, for a term of up to 5 years.  (3) The Governor-General must not appoint a person as a Councillor or Council President unless the Governor-General is satisfied that:  (a) the person qualifies for the appointment because of the person’s knowledge of, or experience in, industry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or public administration; and  (b) a majority of the States and Territories that are parties to the Competition Principles Agreement support the appointment."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e91d7a15b861657c33384cf518ea3a474771c60d4d99e8ca098f1181cc1bb0d0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "95"^^xsd:integer ;
