doc:sec-29l-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "29L(7) Council meetings" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) At a meeting, a question must be decided by a majority of votes of the Councillors present and voting. The Councillor presiding has a deliberative vote, and a casting vote if the deliberative votes are equally divided." ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29LA Resolutions without meetings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-29la ;
    values:originalText "(1) If all Councillors (other than those that must not sign a document because of subsection (3)) sign a document containing a statement that they are in favour of a resolution in terms set out in the document, then a resolution in those terms is taken to have been passed at a duly constituted meeting of the Council held on the day the document was signed, or, if the members sign the document on different days, on the last of those days.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 The National Competition Council  Part IIA  Section 29M  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), 2 or more separate documents containing statements in identical terms each of which is signed by one or more Councillors are together taken to constitute one document containing a statement in those terms signed by those Councillors on the respective days on which they signed the separate documents.  (3) A Councillor must not sign a document containing a statement in favour of a resolution if the resolution concerns a matter in which the Councillor has any pecuniary interest, being an interest that could conflict with the proper performance of the Councillor’s functions in relation to any matter." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If all Councillors (other than those that must not sign a document because of subsection (3)) sign a document containing a statement that they are in favour of a resolution in terms set out in the document, then a resolution in those terms is taken to have been passed at a duly constituted meeting of the Council held on the day the document was signed, or, if the members sign the document on different days, on the last of those days.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 The National Competition Council  Part IIA  Section 29M  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), 2 or more separate documents containing statements in identical terms each of which is signed by one or more Councillors are together taken to constitute one document containing a statement in those terms signed by those Councillors on the respective days on which they signed the separate documents.  (3) A Councillor must not sign a document containing a statement in favour of a resolution if the resolution concerns a matter in which the Councillor has any pecuniary interest, being an interest that could conflict with the proper performance of the Councillor’s functions in relation to any matter."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "77885d93cac8bb732143e1477a20623679b92e94a27782018b3b502e0c53d1e4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-29la-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
