concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44am a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44AM Appointment of Commonwealth AER members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44am ;
    values:originalText "(1) A Commonwealth AER member is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument, on either a full-time or part-time basis. Note: A Commonwealth AER member is also taken to be an associate member of the Commission: see section 8AB.  (2) A Commonwealth AER member holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5 years.  (3) A person is not eligible for appointment as a Commonwealth AER member unless the person has knowledge of, or experience in, industry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or public administration." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A Commonwealth AER member is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument, on either a full-time or part-time basis. Note: A Commonwealth AER member is also taken to be an associate member of the Commission: see section 8AB.  (2) A Commonwealth AER member holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5 years.  (3) A person is not eligible for appointment as a Commonwealth AER member unless the person has knowledge of, or experience in, industry, commerce, economics, law, consumer protection or public administration."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "35b73ecd6554f5c52b56851b75ac3250c8462a097830b5b8677bcf11c8f9b84c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer ;
