doc:sec-44ar-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44AR(4) AER Chair" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If a person who is the AER Deputy Chair ceases to be an AER member, then the person also ceases to be the AER Deputy Chair.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)  Part IIIAA Administrative provisions relating to the AER  Division 4  Section 44ARB  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Note: A person may cease to be the AER Deputy Chair without ceasing to be an AER member. 44ARB  AER Deputy Chair to act as the AER Chair  The AER Deputy Chair is to act as the AER Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of the AER Chair, whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office; or  (b) during all periods when the AER Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: See also subsection 33A(2) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    cof:pageNumber "118"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44as a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44AS Acting AER Deputy Chair"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44as ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint an AER member to act as the AER Deputy Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of the AER Deputy Chair, whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office; or  (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the AER Deputy Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) If a person acting as the AER Deputy Chair ceases to be an AER member, then the appointment to act as the AER Deputy Chair also ceases.  Chapter 1  Preliminary Part IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint an AER member to act as the AER Deputy Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of the AER Deputy Chair, whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office; or  (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the AER Deputy Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) If a person acting as the AER Deputy Chair ceases to be an AER member, then the appointment to act as the AER Deputy Chair also ceases.  Chapter 1  Preliminary Part IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "67bb385740b6e677625ebcbe7fb985c4bce550b0bb1f0597cc65e9058623a1b4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "119"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44as-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44as-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.119" .
doc:sec-44as a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44AS Acting AER Deputy Chair" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by written instrument, appoint an AER member to act as the AER Deputy Chair:  (a) during a vacancy in the office of the AER Deputy Chair, whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office; or  (b) during any period, or during all periods, when the AER Deputy Chair:  (i) is absent from duty or from Australia; or  (ii) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office. Note: For rules that apply to acting appointments, see sections 33AB and 33A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) If a person acting as the AER Deputy Chair ceases to be an AER member, then the appointment to act as the AER Deputy Chair also ceases.  Chapter 1  Preliminary Part IIIAA  The Australian Energy Regulator (AER)" ;
    cof:pageNumber "119"^^xsd:integer .

