concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44at a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44AT Remuneration of AER members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44at ;
    values:originalText "(1) An AER member is to be paid the remuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of that remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, the member is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed.  (2) An AER member is to be paid the allowances that are prescribed.  (3) Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act 1973." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An AER member is to be paid the remuneration that is determined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of that remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, the member is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed.  (2) An AER member is to be paid the allowances that are prescribed.  (3) Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to the Remuneration Tribunal Act 1973."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4a1204efed2740119c34bb963a85972de01352fbd3c9b40b945e9222f8ae45c9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44at-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44at-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44at-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.120" .
