doc:sec-44ha-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44HA(4) Designated Minister must publish his or her decision" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The designated Minister must have regard to any submission so made in deciding what to publish. He or she may have regard to any other matter he or she considers relevant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44i a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44I Duration and effect of declaration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44i ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to this section, a declaration begins to operate at a time specified in the declaration. The time cannot be earlier than 21 days after the declaration is published.  (2) If:  (a) an application for review of a declaration is made within 21 days after the day the declaration is published; and  (b) the Tribunal makes an order under section 44KA staying the operation of the declaration; the declaration does not begin to operate until the order is no longer of effect under subsection 44KA(6) or the Tribunal makes a  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to this section, a declaration begins to operate at a time specified in the declaration. The time cannot be earlier than 21 days after the declaration is published.  (2) If:  (a) an application for review of a declaration is made within 21 days after the day the declaration is published; and  (b) the Tribunal makes an order under section 44KA staying the operation of the declaration; the declaration does not begin to operate until the order is no longer of effect under subsection 44KA(6) or the Tribunal makes a  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
