    cml:conclusionText "the declaration's operation is allowed before the tribunal's decision" ;
    cml:executionSurface "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser" ;
    cml:confidence "0.5000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-44ka-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44KA(1) Tribunal may stay operation of declaration" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to this section, an application for review of a declaration under subsection 44K(1) does not:  (a) affect the operation of the declaration; or  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Declared services  Division 2  Section 44KA  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (b) prevent the taking of steps in reliance on the declaration." ;
    cof:pageNumber "160"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ka-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44KA(2) Tribunal may stay operation of declaration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44ka-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) On application by a person who has been made a party to the proceedings for review of a declaration, the Tribunal may:  (a) make an order staying, or otherwise affecting the operation or the taking of steps in reliance on, the declaration if the Tribunal considers that:  (i) it is desirable to make the order after taking into account the interests of any person who may be affected by the review; and  (ii) the order is appropriate for the purpose of securing the effectiveness of the hearing and determination of the application for review; or  (b) make an order varying or revoking an order made under paragraph (a) (including an order that has previously been varied on one or more occasions under this paragraph)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) On application by a person who has been made a party to the proceedings for review of a declaration, the Tribunal may:  (a) make an order staying, or otherwise affecting the operation or the taking of steps in reliance on, the declaration if the Tribunal considers that:  (i) it is desirable to make the order after taking into account the interests of any person who may be affected by the review; and  (ii) the order is appropriate for the purpose of securing the effectiveness of the hearing and determination of the application for review; or  (b) make an order varying or revoking an order made under paragraph (a) (including an order that has previously been varied on one or more occasions under this paragraph)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "83ec3022bd56c69cc18ea3f0cbb709aed0f29a08dcb4c8601c57fb2d2204e796" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ka ;
    cof:pageNumber "160"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Tribunal may stay operation of declaration on application by a party to proceedings for review." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
