concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44LG(6) Designated Minister’s decision on ineligibility"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44lg-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44LH his or her decision on the ineligibility recommendation within the period starting at the start of the day the recommendation is received and ending at the end of 60 days after that day:  (a) the designated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of that 60-day period, to have made a decision under subsection (1) in accordance with the ineligibility recommendation and to have published that decision under section 44LH; and  (b) if the Council recommended that the designated Minister decide that the service be ineligible to be a declared service—the period for which the decision is in force is taken to be the period recommended by the Council.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "(6) If the designated Minister does not publish under section 44LH his or her decision on the ineligibility recommendation within the period starting at the start of the day the recommendation is received and ending at the end of 60 days after that day:  (a) the designated Minister is taken, immediately after the end of that 60-day period, to have made a decision under subsection (1) in accordance with the ineligibility recommendation and to have published that decision under section 44LH; and  (b) if the Council recommended that the designated Minister decide that the service be ineligible to be a declared service—the period for which the decision is in force is taken to be the period recommended by the Council.  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e7265d7a9662630255c645710babc3624d842de16bbc2803a4c5d97132ecd026" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lg ;
    cof:pageNumber "172"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Designated Minister must publish decision on ineligibility within 60 days." ;
