doc:sec-44li-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44LI(1) Revocation of ineligibility decision" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Council may recommend to the designated Minister that the designated Minister revoke his or her decision (the ineligibility  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Services that are ineligible to be declared  Division 2AA  Section 44LI  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  decision) that a service is ineligible to be a declared service. The Council must have regard to the objects of this Part in making its recommendation." ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44li-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44LI(2) Revocation of ineligibility decision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44li-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Council cannot recommend that a decision be revoked unless:  (a) it is satisfied that, at the time of the recommendation, the facility that is (or will be) used to provide the service concerned is so materially different from the proposed facility described in the application made under section 44LB that the Council is satisfied of all of the declaration criteria for the service; or  (b) the person who is, or expects to be, the provider of the service that is provided, or that is proposed to be provided, by means of the facility requests that it be revoked. Minister must decide whether to revoke" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The Council cannot recommend that a decision be revoked unless:  (a) it is satisfied that, at the time of the recommendation, the facility that is (or will be) used to provide the service concerned is so materially different from the proposed facility described in the application made under section 44LB that the Council is satisfied of all of the declaration criteria for the service; or  (b) the person who is, or expects to be, the provider of the service that is provided, or that is proposed to be provided, by means of the facility requests that it be revoked. Minister must decide whether to revoke"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4bc1c2b19e67224ec35b5a06117a75aa78622c261da366fd6180d7739449afa4" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44li ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Council must decide whether to revoke decision" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.174" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44li-ss-2-norm .
