concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44li-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44LI(6) Revocation of ineligibility decision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44li-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If the designated Minister decides not to revoke the ineligibility decision, the designated Minister must give reasons for the decision to the person who is, or expects to be, the provider of the service concerned when the designated Minister publishes the decision.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "(6) If the designated Minister decides not to revoke the ineligibility decision, the designated Minister must give reasons for the decision to the person who is, or expects to be, the provider of the service concerned when the designated Minister publishes the decision.  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "34e36d577a40bcbad7fac96680dcacdefc0d21a00c42a892880a113e5bd3e423" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44li ;
