concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44lk-ss-9 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44LK(9) Review of decision to revoke or not revoke an ineligibility"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44lk-ss-9 ;
    values:originalText "(9) If the designated Minister decided not to revoke his or her ineligibility decision, the Tribunal may either:  (a) affirm the designated Minister’s decision; or  (b) set aside the designated Minister’s decision and revoke the ineligibility decision.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "(9) If the designated Minister decided not to revoke his or her ineligibility decision, the Tribunal may either:  (a) affirm the designated Minister’s decision; or  (b) set aside the designated Minister’s decision and revoke the ineligibility decision.  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
