doc:sec-44na-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44NA(5) Recommendation by Council" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) If the Council is satisfied that it is an effective access regime, the Council must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth Minister that he or she extend the period for which the decision under section 44N is in force. The Council must also recommend an extension period." ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44NA(6) Recommendation by Council"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44na-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If the Council is satisfied that it is not an effective access regime, the Council must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth Minister that he or she not extend the period for which the decision under section 44N is in force.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Effective access regimes  Division 2A  Section 44NAA  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Note 1: There are time limits that apply to the Council’s recommendation: see section 44NC. Note 2: The Council may request information and invite public submissions on the application: see sections 44NAA and 44NE. Note 3: The Council must publish its recommendation: see section 44NF. 44NAA  Council may request information" ;
    skos:definition "(6) If the Council is satisfied that it is not an effective access regime, the Council must, in writing, recommend to the Commonwealth Minister that he or she not extend the period for which the decision under section 44N is in force.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Effective access regimes  Division 2A  Section 44NAA  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Note 1: There are time limits that apply to the Council’s recommendation: see section 44NC. Note 2: The Council may request information and invite public submissions on the application: see sections 44NAA and 44NE. Note 3: The Council must publish its recommendation: see section 44NF. 44NAA  Council may request information"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "47ac1092637ce8bf358f0a66fc9f328a5735d2dab18620560f1531f2964fe633" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44na ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Council must recommend not extending period for decision under section 44N if it is not an effective access regime." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.184" ;
