concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ne a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44NE Council may invite public submissions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44ne ;
    values:originalText "Invitation  (1) The Council may publish, by electronic or other means, a notice inviting public submissions on an application under section 44M, 44NA or 44NBA, or on a consideration by the Council on its own initiative under section 44NBA, if it considers that it is appropriate and practicable to do so.  (2) The notice must specify how submissions may be made and the day by which submissions may be made (which must be at least 14 days after the day the notice is published).  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Effective access regimes  Division 2A  Section 44NE  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Consideration of submissions  (3) Subject to subsection (6), in deciding what recommendation to make, the Council:  (a) must have regard to any submission made on or before the day specified in the notice; and  (b) may disregard any submission made after the day specified in the notice. Council may make submissions publicly available  (4) The Council may make any written submission, or a written record (which may be a summary) of any oral submission, publicly available. Confidentiality  (5) A person may, at the time of making a submission, request that the Council:  (a) not make the whole or a part of the submission available under subsection (4); and  (b) not publish or make available the whole or a part of the submission under section 44NF; because of the confidential commercial information contained in the submission.  (6) If the Council refuses such a request:  (a) for a written submission—the Council must, if the person who made it so requires, return the whole or the part of it to the person; and  (b) for an oral submission—the person who made it may inform the Council that the person withdraws the whole or the part of it; and  (c) if the Council returns the whole or the part of the submission, or the person withdraws the whole or the part of the submission, the Council must not:  (i) make the whole or the part of the submission available under subsection (4); and  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "Invitation  (1) The Council may publish, by electronic or other means, a notice inviting public submissions on an application under section 44M, 44NA or 44NBA, or on a consideration by the Council on its own initiative under section 44NBA, if it considers that it is appropriate and practicable to do so.  (2) The notice must specify how submissions may be made and the day by which submissions may be made (which must be at least 14 days after the day the notice is published).  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Effective access regimes  Division 2A  Section 44NE  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Consideration of submissions  (3) Subject to subsection (6), in deciding what recommendation to make, the Council:  (a) must have regard to any submission made on or before the day specified in the notice; and  (b) may disregard any submission made after the day specified in the notice. Council may make submissions publicly available  (4) The Council may make any written submission, or a written record (which may be a summary) of any oral submission, publicly available. Confidentiality  (5) A person may, at the time of making a submission, request that the Council:  (a) not make the whole or a part of the submission available under subsection (4); and  (b) not publish or make available the whole or a part of the submission under section 44NF; because of the confidential commercial information contained in the submission.  (6) If the Council refuses such a request:  (a) for a written submission—the Council must, if the person who made it so requires, return the whole or the part of it to the person; and  (b) for an oral submission—the person who made it may inform the Council that the person withdraws the whole or the part of it; and  (c) if the Council returns the whole or the part of the submission, or the person withdraws the whole or the part of the submission, the Council must not:  (i) make the whole or the part of"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "af4ea02852eb08ea7b96b093b59e744da12779a5997fd70804d7068c90a7cda0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "192"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ne-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ne-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44ne-ss-3 ;
