doc:sec-44pc a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44PC Revocation of approval decision" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Discretionary revocation  (1) The Commission may, by writing, revoke a decision to approve a tender process as a competitive tender process if it is satisfied that the assessment of the tenders was not in accordance with that process.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    cof:pageNumber "201"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44PD Time limit for Commission decisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44pd ;
    values:originalText "Commission to make decision within 90 days  (1) The Commission must make a decision on an application under subsection 44PA(1) within the period of 90 days (the expected period) starting at the start of the day the application is received. Stopping the clock  (2) In working out the expected period in relation to a decision on an application under subsection 44PA(1), in a situation referred to in column 1 of an item of the following table, disregard any day in a period:  (a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of the item; and  (b) ending on the day referred to in column 3 of the item.  Stopping the clock Item Column 1 Situation Column 2 Start day Column 3 End day An agreement is made in relation to the application under subsection (4) The first day of the period specified in the agreement The last day of the period specified in the agreement  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "Commission to make decision within 90 days  (1) The Commission must make a decision on an application under subsection 44PA(1) within the period of 90 days (the expected period) starting at the start of the day the application is received. Stopping the clock  (2) In working out the expected period in relation to a decision on an application under subsection 44PA(1), in a situation referred to in column 1 of an item of the following table, disregard any day in a period:  (a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of the item; and  (b) ending on the day referred to in column 3 of the item.  Stopping the clock Item Column 1 Situation Column 2 Start day Column 3 End day An agreement is made in relation to the application under subsection (4) The first day of the period specified in the agreement The last day of the period specified in the agreement  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "627a20a4ff037c4eed4da8fcfd67bc4ac9af04e8ccd1ae2ed1a8126c8198ac13" ;
    cof:pageNumber "203"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pd-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44pd-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.203" .
doc:sec-44pd a cof:Section ;
