doc:sec-44t-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44T(1) Withdrawal of notifications" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A notification may be withdrawn as follows (and not otherwise):  (a) if the provider notified the dispute:  (i) the provider may withdraw the notification at any time before the Commission makes its final determination;  (ii) the third party may withdraw the provider’s notification at any time after the Commission issues a draft final determination, but before it makes its final determination;  (b) if the third party notified the dispute, the third party may withdraw the notification at any time before the Commission makes its final determination." ;
    cof:pageNumber "213"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44T(2) Withdrawal of notifications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44t-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Despite subparagraph (1)(a)(ii), if the provider notified a dispute over variation of a final determination, the third party may not withdraw the provider’s notification." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Despite subparagraph (1)(a)(ii), if the provider notified a dispute over variation of a final determination, the third party may not withdraw the provider’s notification."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "35441ca5bcf457a186bab96f6aaff0f694c26066a610ad16e41bfb14f6113ea2" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44t ;
    cof:pageNumber "213"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Third party cannot withdraw provider's notification despite dispute over variation of final determination." ;
