doc:sec-44v a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44V Determination by Commission" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Unless it terminates the arbitration under section 44Y, 44YA, 44ZZCB or 44ZZCBA, the Commission:  (a) must make a written final determination; and  (b) may make a written interim determination;  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    cof:pageNumber "213"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44w a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44W Restrictions on access determinations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44w ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission must not make a determination that would have any of the following effects:  (a) preventing an existing user obtaining a sufficient amount of the service to be able to meet the user’s reasonably anticipated requirements, measured at the time when the dispute was notified;  (b) preventing a person from obtaining, by the exercise of a pre-notification right, a sufficient amount of the service to be able to meet the person’s actual requirements;  (c) depriving any person of a protected contractual right;  (d) resulting in the third party becoming the owner (or one of the owners) of any part of the facility, or of extensions of the facility (including expansions of the capacity of the facility and expansions of the geographical reach of the facility), without the consent of the provider;  (e) requiring the provider to bear some or all of the costs of extending the facility (including expanding the capacity of the facility and expanding the geographical reach of the facility);  (ea) requiring the provider to bear some or all of the costs of maintaining extensions of the facility (including expansions of the capacity of the facility and expansions of the geographical reach of the facility);  (f) requiring the provider to bear some or all of the costs of interconnections to the facility or maintaining interconnections to the facility.  (2) Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply in relation to the requirements and rights of the third party and the provider when the Commission is making a determination in arbitration of an access dispute relating to an earlier determination of an access dispute between the third party and the provider.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission must not make a determination that would have any of the following effects:  (a) preventing an existing user obtaining a sufficient amount of the service to be able to meet the user’s reasonably anticipated requirements, measured at the time when the dispute was notified;  (b) preventing a person from obtaining, by the exercise of a pre-notification right, a sufficient amount of the service to be able to meet the person’s actual requirements;  (c) depriving any person of a protected contractual right;  (d) resulting in the third party becoming the owner (or one of the owners) of any part of the facility, or of extensions of the facility (including expansions of the capacity of the facility and expansions of the geographical reach of the facility), without the consent of the provider;  (e) requiring the provider to bear some or all of the costs of extending the facility (including expanding the capacity of the facility and expanding the geographical reach of the facility);  (ea) requiring the provider to bear some or all of the costs of maintaining extensions of the facility (including expansions of the capacity of the facility and expansions of the geographical reach of the facility);  (f) requiring the provider to bear some or all of the costs of interconnections to the facility or maintaining interconnections to the facility.  (2) Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply in relation to the requirements and rights of the third party and the provider when the Commission is making a determination in arbitration of an access dispute relating to an earlier determination of an access dispute between the third party and the provider.  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0cb1929705bb63fe8fe85e38fa8c29f8e052c2620e74c52bf0b9a17f8326ed08" ;
    cof:pageNumber "215"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44w-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44w-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.215" .
