concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZF Procedure of Commission"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zf ;
    values:originalText "(1) In an arbitration hearing about an access dispute, the Commission:  (a) is not bound by technicalities, legal forms or rules of evidence; and  (b) must act as speedily as a proper consideration of the dispute allows, having regard to the need to carefully and quickly inquire into and investigate the dispute and all matters affecting the merits, and fair settlement, of the dispute; and  (c) may inform itself of any matter relevant to the dispute in any way it thinks appropriate.  (2) The Commission may determine the periods that are reasonably necessary for the fair and adequate presentation of the respective cases of the parties to an access dispute, and may require that the cases be presented within those periods.  (3) The Commission may require evidence or argument to be presented in writing, and may decide the matters on which it will hear oral evidence or argument.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZG  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) In an arbitration hearing about an access dispute, the Commission:  (a) is not bound by technicalities, legal forms or rules of evidence; and  (b) must act as speedily as a proper consideration of the dispute allows, having regard to the need to carefully and quickly inquire into and investigate the dispute and all matters affecting the merits, and fair settlement, of the dispute; and  (c) may inform itself of any matter relevant to the dispute in any way it thinks appropriate.  (2) The Commission may determine the periods that are reasonably necessary for the fair and adequate presentation of the respective cases of the parties to an access dispute, and may require that the cases be presented within those periods.  (3) The Commission may require evidence or argument to be presented in writing, and may decide the matters on which it will hear oral evidence or argument.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZG  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "29379897601443f309e6e97910b0c34887d2e884ed97e3df7ddc97aebff8c46b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zf-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.222" .
doc:sec-44zf a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44ZF Procedure of Commission" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) In an arbitration hearing about an access dispute, the Commission:  (a) is not bound by technicalities, legal forms or rules of evidence; and  (b) must act as speedily as a proper consideration of the dispute allows, having regard to the need to carefully and quickly inquire into and investigate the dispute and all matters affecting the merits, and fair settlement, of the dispute; and  (c) may inform itself of any matter relevant to the dispute in any way it thinks appropriate.  (2) The Commission may determine the periods that are reasonably necessary for the fair and adequate presentation of the respective cases of the parties to an access dispute, and may require that the cases be presented within those periods.  (3) The Commission may require evidence or argument to be presented in writing, and may decide the matters on which it will hear oral evidence or argument.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZG  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer .

