doc:sec-44zh a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44ZH Power to take evidence on oath or affirmation" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may take evidence on oath or affirmation and for that purpose a member of the Commission may administer an oath or affirmation.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    cof:pageNumber "223"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zi a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZI Failing to attend as a witness"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zi ;
    values:originalText "A person who is served, as prescribed, with a summons to appear as a witness before the Commission must not, without reasonable excuse:  (a) fail to attend as required by the summons; or  (b) fail to appear and report himself or herself from day to day unless excused, or released from further attendance, by a member of the Commission. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. 44ZJ  Failing to answer questions etc.  (1) A person appearing as a witness before the Commission must not, without reasonable excuse:  (a) refuse or fail to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or  (b) refuse or fail to answer a question that the person is required to answer by the Commission; or  (c) refuse or fail to produce a document that he or she was required to produce by a summons under this Part served on him or her as prescribed. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.  (2) It is a reasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1) for an individual to refuse or fail to answer a question or produce a document on the ground that the answer or the production of the document might tend to incriminate the individual or to expose the individual to a penalty. This subsection does not limit what is a reasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1).  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZK  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    skos:definition "A person who is served, as prescribed, with a summons to appear as a witness before the Commission must not, without reasonable excuse:  (a) fail to attend as required by the summons; or  (b) fail to appear and report himself or herself from day to day unless excused, or released from further attendance, by a member of the Commission. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. 44ZJ  Failing to answer questions etc.  (1) A person appearing as a witness before the Commission must not, without reasonable excuse:  (a) refuse or fail to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or  (b) refuse or fail to answer a question that the person is required to answer by the Commission; or  (c) refuse or fail to produce a document that he or she was required to produce by a summons under this Part served on him or her as prescribed. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.  (2) It is a reasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1) for an individual to refuse or fail to answer a question or produce a document on the ground that the answer or the production of the document might tend to incriminate the individual or to expose the individual to a penalty. This subsection does not limit what is a reasonable excuse for the purposes of subsection (1).  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZK  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b2a2466c6982c4164ec946b815c312c8b5d7b6190392f8b9c6470a33f740f907" ;
    cof:pageNumber "224"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zi-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zi-ss-2 ;
