    values:originalText "(1) A party to an arbitration hearing may:  (a) inform the Commission that, in the party’s opinion, a specified part of a document contains confidential commercial information; and  (b) request the Commission not to give a copy of that part to another party." ;
    cof:pageNumber "225"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zl-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZL(2) Party may request Commission to treat material as"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zl-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) On receiving a request, the Commission must:  (a) inform the other party or parties that the request has been made and of the general nature of the matters to which the relevant part of the document relates; and  (b) ask the other party or parties whether there is any objection to the Commission complying with the request." ;
    skos:definition "(2) On receiving a request, the Commission must:  (a) inform the other party or parties that the request has been made and of the general nature of the matters to which the relevant part of the document relates; and  (b) ask the other party or parties whether there is any objection to the Commission complying with the request."@en ;
