doc:sec-44zn-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44ZN(2) Parties to pay costs of an arbitration" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Chairperson may do so only if he or she considers this would be likely to result in the nominated disputes being resolved in a more efficient and timely manner.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZNA  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Consulting the parties" ;
    cof:pageNumber "226"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zn-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZN(3) Parties to pay costs of an arbitration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zn-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Before doing so, the Chairperson must give each party to the arbitration of each nominated dispute a notice in writing:  (a) specifying what the Chairperson is proposing to do; and  (b) inviting the party to make a written submission on the proposal to the Chairperson within 14 days after the notice is given." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Before doing so, the Chairperson must give each party to the arbitration of each nominated dispute a notice in writing:  (a) specifying what the Chairperson is proposing to do; and  (b) inviting the party to make a written submission on the proposal to the Chairperson within 14 days after the notice is given."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5eb9d5a75617afdc1c2c87ae70287283bccdac019a833b6b1eaaf4df8f2b3954" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zn ;
    cof:pageNumber "226"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Chairperson must give notice to parties before doing something" ;
    dc:description "written submission within 14 days" ;
