concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZT Transmission of documents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zt ;
    values:originalText "If an appeal is instituted in the Federal Court:  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZU  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the Tribunal must send to the Federal Court all documents that were before the Tribunal in connection with the matter to which the appeal relates; and  (b) at the conclusion of the proceedings before the Federal Court in relation to the appeal, the Federal Court must return the documents to the Tribunal. Subdivision G—Variation and revocation of determinations" ;
    skos:definition "If an appeal is instituted in the Federal Court:  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZU  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the Tribunal must send to the Federal Court all documents that were before the Tribunal in connection with the matter to which the appeal relates; and  (b) at the conclusion of the proceedings before the Federal Court in relation to the appeal, the Federal Court must return the documents to the Tribunal. Subdivision G—Variation and revocation of determinations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9157ef8890d17671e944bd074a05bf9559a9096c4d96738009e56941983ebfe7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "234"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Transmission of documents in Federal Court proceedings" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.234" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt-norm .
concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt-norm a values:Undertaking ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zt ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-44zt a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44ZT Transmission of documents" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If an appeal is instituted in the Federal Court:  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Access to declared services  Division 3  Section 44ZU  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the Tribunal must send to the Federal Court all documents that were before the Tribunal in connection with the matter to which the appeal relates; and  (b) at the conclusion of the proceedings before the Federal Court in relation to the appeal, the Federal Court must return the documents to the Tribunal. Subdivision G—Variation and revocation of determinations" ;
    cof:pageNumber "234"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZU Variation of final determinations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zu ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may vary a final determination on the application of any party to the determination. However, it cannot vary the final determination if any other party objects. Note: If the parties cannot agree on a variation, a new access dispute can be notified under section 44S.  (2) Sections 44W and 44X apply to a variation under this section as if:  (a) an access dispute arising out of the final determination had been notified when the application was made to the Commission for the variation of the determination; and  (b) the variation were the making of a final determination in the terms of the varied determination. 44ZUA  Variation and revocation of interim determinations  (1) The Commission may, by writing, vary or revoke an interim determination.  (2) The Commission must, by writing, revoke an interim determination if requested to do so by the parties to the determination.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may vary a final determination on the application of any party to the determination. However, it cannot vary the final determination if any other party objects. Note: If the parties cannot agree on a variation, a new access dispute can be notified under section 44S.  (2) Sections 44W and 44X apply to a variation under this section as if:  (a) an access dispute arising out of the final determination had been notified when the application was made to the Commission for the variation of the determination; and  (b) the variation were the making of a final determination in the terms of the varied determination. 44ZUA  Variation and revocation of interim determinations  (1) The Commission may, by writing, vary or revoke an interim determination.  (2) The Commission must, by writing, revoke an interim determination if requested to do so by the parties to the determination.  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "43e464a7c80a40928d32dbd3d1f15e361a2ddd31a0d4b382aa70b7742a121d50" ;
    cof:pageNumber "235"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zu-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
