    cof:title "44ZV Constitutional limits on operation of this Division" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "This Division does not apply to a contract unless:  (a) the contract provides for access to a declared service; and  (b) the contract was made after the service was declared; and  (c) the parties to the contract are the provider of the service and a third party; and  (d) at least one of the following conditions is met:  (i) the provider is a corporation (or a partnership or joint venture consisting wholly of corporations);  (ii) the third party is a corporation;  (iii) the access is (or would be) in the course of, or for the purposes of, constitutional trade or commerce." ;
    cof:pageNumber "236"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZW Registration of contract"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zw ;
    values:originalText "(1) On application by all the parties to a contract, the Commission must:  (a) register the contract by entering the following details on a public register:  (i) the names of the parties to the contract;  (ii) the service to which the contract relates;  (iii) the date on which the contract was made; or  (b) decide not to register the contract.  (2) In deciding whether to register a contract, the Commission must take into account:  (aa) the objects of this Part; and  (a) the public interest, including the public interest in having competition in markets (whether or not in Australia); and  (b) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service to which the contract relates.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Registered contracts for access to declared services  Division 4  Section 44ZX  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (2A) The Commission must not register a contract if it deals with a matter or matters relating to access to the service that are dealt with in an access undertaking that is in operation.  (3) The Commission must publish a decision not to register a contract.  (4) If the Commission publishes a decision not to register a contract, it must give the parties to the contract reasons for the decision when it publishes the decision." ;
    skos:definition "(1) On application by all the parties to a contract, the Commission must:  (a) register the contract by entering the following details on a public register:  (i) the names of the parties to the contract;  (ii) the service to which the contract relates;  (iii) the date on which the contract was made; or  (b) decide not to register the contract.  (2) In deciding whether to register a contract, the Commission must take into account:  (aa) the objects of this Part; and  (a) the public interest, including the public interest in having competition in markets (whether or not in Australia); and  (b) the interests of all persons who have rights to use the service to which the contract relates.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Registered contracts for access to declared services  Division 4  Section 44ZX  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (2A) The Commission must not register a contract if it deals with a matter or matters relating to access to the service that are dealt with in an access undertaking that is in operation.  (3) The Commission must publish a decision not to register a contract.  (4) If the Commission publishes a decision not to register a contract, it must give the parties to the contract reasons for the decision when it publishes the decision."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66a6d6a80affb7fec2f3d684544e3b1e1269e336007af51ff7418d0c42b842c7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "236"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zw-ss-2a ;
