doc:sec-44zy a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44ZY Effect of registration of contract" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The parties to a contract that has been registered:  (a) may enforce the contract under Division 7 as if the contract were a determination of the Commission under section 44V and they were parties to the determination; and  (b) cannot enforce the contract by any other means.  Access to services  Chapter 2 Access to services  Part IIIA Hindering access to declared services  Division 5  Section 44ZZ  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "238"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44ZZ Prohibition on hindering access to declared services"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44zz ;
    values:originalText "(1) The provider or a user of a service to which a third party has access under a determination, or a body corporate related to the provider or a user of the service, must not engage in conduct for the purpose of preventing or hindering the third party’s access to the service under the determination.  (2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose referred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has been considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only by inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant circumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which the purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of subsection (1).  (3) In this section, a user of a service includes a person who has a right to use the service.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The provider or a user of a service to which a third party has access under a determination, or a body corporate related to the provider or a user of the service, must not engage in conduct for the purpose of preventing or hindering the third party’s access to the service under the determination.  (2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose referred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has been considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only by inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant circumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which the purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of subsection (1).  (3) In this section, a user of a service includes a person who has a right to use the service.  Chapter 2  Access to services"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5425a0820c5cbfa76775d80b0fe7ff0438cb6c67a7cbe4ffea0df775cf2e7f82" ;
    cof:pageNumber "239"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-44zz-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.239" .
doc:sec-44zz a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44ZZ Prohibition on hindering access to declared services" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The provider or a user of a service to which a third party has access under a determination, or a body corporate related to the provider or a user of the service, must not engage in conduct for the purpose of preventing or hindering the third party’s access to the service under the determination.  (2) A person may be taken to have engaged in conduct for the purpose referred to in subsection (1) even though, after all the evidence has been considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only by inference from the conduct of the person or from other relevant circumstances. This subsection does not limit the manner in which the purpose of a person may be established for the purposes of subsection (1).  (3) In this section, a user of a service includes a person who has a right to use the service.  Chapter 2  Access to services" ;
    cof:pageNumber "239"^^xsd:integer .

