concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ah a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45AH Determining guilt"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-45ah ;
    values:originalText "(1) A corporation may be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG even if:  (a) each other party to the contract, arrangement or understanding is a person who is not criminally responsible; or  (b) subject to subsection (2), all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of the offence. Note: Party has an extended meaning—see section 45AC.  (2) A corporation cannot be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG if:  (a) all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of such an offence; and  (b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A corporation may be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG even if:  (a) each other party to the contract, arrangement or understanding is a person who is not criminally responsible; or  (b) subject to subsection (2), all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of the offence. Note: Party has an extended meaning—see section 45AC.  (2) A corporation cannot be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG if:  (a) all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of such an offence; and  (b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7a83b2d57870ad22e66ccfcf8c253e01e0f76740870ce4a52c19c608eda0885b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "293"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ah-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45ah-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.293" .
doc:sec-45ah a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45AH Determining guilt" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A corporation may be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG even if:  (a) each other party to the contract, arrangement or understanding is a person who is not criminally responsible; or  (b) subject to subsection (2), all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of the offence. Note: Party has an extended meaning—see section 45AC.  (2) A corporation cannot be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG if:  (a) all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of such an offence; and  (b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal." ;
    cof:pageNumber "293"^^xsd:integer .

