    skos:definition "(2) A corporation cannot be found guilty of an offence against section 45AF or 45AG if:  (a) all other parties to the contract, arrangement or understanding have been acquitted of such an offence; and  (b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal."@en ;
