doc:sec-45dc a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45DC Involvement and liability of employee organisations" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Certain organisations taken to be acting in concert  (1) If 2 or more persons (the participants), each of whom is a member or officer of the same organisation of employees, engage in conduct in concert with one another, whether or not the conduct is also engaged in in concert with another person, then, unless the organisation proves otherwise, the organisation is taken for the purposes of sections 45D, 45DA and 45DB:  (a) to engage in that conduct in concert with the participants; and  (b) to have engaged in that conduct for the purposes for which the participants engaged in it.  Chapter 3  Restrictive trade practices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "313"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45DD Situations in which boycotts permitted"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-45dd ;
    values:originalText "Dominant purpose of conduct relates to employment matters— conduct by a person  (1) A person does not contravene, and is not involved in a contravention of, subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1) or 45DB(1) by engaging in conduct if the dominant purpose for which the conduct is engaged in is substantially related to the remuneration, conditions of employment, hours of work or working conditions of that person or of another person employed by an employer of that person.  Chapter 3  Restrictive trade practices" ;
    skos:definition "Dominant purpose of conduct relates to employment matters— conduct by a person  (1) A person does not contravene, and is not involved in a contravention of, subsection 45D(1), 45DA(1) or 45DB(1) by engaging in conduct if the dominant purpose for which the conduct is engaged in is substantially related to the remuneration, conditions of employment, hours of work or working conditions of that person or of another person employed by an employer of that person.  Chapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b3c254a19b692c8b918b1dba04b978c13ab324a0ddddd84cb787357f7fdba46f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "315"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Boycotts permitted if dominant purpose is related to employment matters" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.315" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-45dd-norm .
