doc:sec-48-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "48(2) Resale price maintenance" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a corporation or other person engaging in conduct that constitutes the practice of resale price maintenance if:  Restrictive trade practices  Chapter 3 Restrictive trade practices  Part IV Other provisions  Division 2  Section 49  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the corporation or other person has given the Commission a notice under subsection 93(1) describing the conduct; and  (b) the notice is in force under section 93." ;
    cof:pageNumber "334"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-49 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49 Dual listed company arrangements that affect competition"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-49 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A corporation must not:  (a) make a dual listed company arrangement if a provision of the proposed arrangement has the purpose, or would have or be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening competition; or  (b) give effect to a provision of a dual listed company arrangement if that provision has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening competition. Note: Conduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be authorised under section 88. Exception  (2) The making by a corporation of a dual listed company arrangement that contains a provision that has the purpose, or would have or be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening competition does not contravene this section if:  (a) the arrangement is subject to a condition that the provision will not come into force unless and until the corporation is granted an authorisation to give effect to the provision; and  (b) the corporation applies for the grant of such an authorisation within 14 days after the arrangement is made. However, this subsection does not permit the corporation to give effect to such a provision. Meaning of competition  (3) For the purposes of this section, competition, in relation to a provision of a dual listed company arrangement or of a proposed dual listed company arrangement, means competition in any market in which:  Chapter 3  Restrictive trade practices" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A corporation must not:  (a) make a dual listed company arrangement if a provision of the proposed arrangement has the purpose, or would have or be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening competition; or  (b) give effect to a provision of a dual listed company arrangement if that provision has the purpose, or has or is likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening competition. Note: Conduct that would otherwise contravene this section can be authorised under section 88. Exception  (2) The making by a corporation of a dual listed company arrangement that contains a provision that has the purpose, or would have or be likely to have the effect, of substantially lessening competition does not contravene this section if:  (a) the arrangement is subject to a condition that the provision will not come into force unless and until the corporation is granted an authorisation to give effect to the provision; and  (b) the corporation applies for the grant of such an authorisation within 14 days after the arrangement is made. However, this subsection does not permit the corporation to give effect to such a provision. Meaning of competition  (3) For the purposes of this section, competition, in relation to a provision of a dual listed company arrangement or of a proposed dual listed company arrangement, means competition in any market in which:  Chapter 3  Restrictive trade practices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "34e3ef35db0166c22fa6bcaa68d5205773e08600d5bafc896a0d95347d78ec1b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "335"^^xsd:integer ;
