    values:originalText "(1A) If regulations prescribe an industry code, the industry code may confer on a person or body functions and powers in relation to the code, including functions and powers in relation to the following matters:  (a) monitoring compliance with the code;  (b) dealing with disputes or complaints arising under, or in relation to, the code;  (c) dealing with matters relating to a prospective agreement (including disputes or complaints relating to such an agreement) that would, if entered into, have the effect that one or more parties to the agreement is a participant in the industry to which the code relates;  (d) conducting investigations under, or in relation to, the code;  (e) providing exemptions from the code or specified provisions of the code;  (f) reviewing, or reporting on, the operation of the code or activities under, or in relation to, the code;  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4 Industry codes  Part IVB Miscellaneous  Division 6  Section 51AE  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (g) any other matter relating to the operation, application or administration of the code." ;
