concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-51ae-ss-1d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "51AE(1D) Regulations relating to industry codes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-51ae-ss-1d ;
    values:originalText "(1D) However, if an industry code confers on a person or body a function of providing, or a power to provide, exemptions from the code or specified provisions of the code, then (despite anything to the contrary in the code):  (a) the function or power must be exercised by written instrument (an exemption instrument); and  (b) if the code does not provide that an exemption instrument made under the code is a legislative instrument, then:  Chapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc." ;
    skos:definition "(1D) However, if an industry code confers on a person or body a function of providing, or a power to provide, exemptions from the code or specified provisions of the code, then (despite anything to the contrary in the code):  (a) the function or power must be exercised by written instrument (an exemption instrument); and  (b) if the code does not provide that an exemption instrument made under the code is a legislative instrument, then:  Chapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "557b233d52b1db5f2ce21e29ce7f8732457acee492f9570d3edd2648457a9660" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-51ae ;
    cof:pageNumber "440"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemptions from industry codes must be exercised through written instruments." ;
    dc:description "Written instrument (exemption instrument)" ;
