concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52h-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "52H(2) Revocation of registration or endorsement—general"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-52h-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The ACMA may revoke the registration of a registered news business if the ACMA considers that any of the following requirements are not met in relation to the news business:  (a) the requirement in subsection 52N(1) (the content test);  (b) the requirement in subsection 52O(1) (the Australian audience test);  (c) the requirement in subsection 52P(1) (the professional standards test)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The ACMA may revoke the registration of a registered news business if the ACMA considers that any of the following requirements are not met in relation to the news business:  (a) the requirement in subsection 52N(1) (the content test);  (b) the requirement in subsection 52O(1) (the Australian audience test);  (c) the requirement in subsection 52P(1) (the professional standards test)."@en ;
