concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "52K Adding or removing news source from registered news business"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-52k ;
    values:originalText "(1) A registered news business corporation for a registered news business may apply to the ACMA for:  (a) the addition of a news source to the news business; or  (b) the removal of a news source from the news business.  (2) The application must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) set out every news source that comprises the news business; and  (c) specify the news source to be added or removed; and  (d) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify requirements—meet those requirements.  (3) The ACMA may add the news source to the news business if the ACMA considers that:  (a) the application is in accordance with subsection (2); and  (b) the news source does not form part of another news business that is a registered news business; and  (c) the corporation would continue to meet the requirement in 52L (connection between applicant corporation and news  Chapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc. Part IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A registered news business corporation for a registered news business may apply to the ACMA for:  (a) the addition of a news source to the news business; or  (b) the removal of a news source from the news business.  (2) The application must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) set out every news source that comprises the news business; and  (c) specify the news source to be added or removed; and  (d) if regulations made for the purposes of this paragraph specify requirements—meet those requirements.  (3) The ACMA may add the news source to the news business if the ACMA considers that:  (a) the application is in accordance with subsection (2); and  (b) the news source does not form part of another news business that is a registered news business; and  (c) the corporation would continue to meet the requirement in 52L (connection between applicant corporation and news  Chapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc. Part IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8e0a93946b1fdd1076b530e9154da10c66768a41422bdf76849a9da8c878a1ee" ;
    cof:pageNumber "457"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52k-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52k-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52k-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
