concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zk a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "52ZK Register of bargaining code arbitrators"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-52zk ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA must establish and keep a register of bargaining code arbitrators.  (2) Each such person listed on the register must be:  (a) a person experienced in legal matters, economic matters or industry matters; or  (b) a person who the ACMA considers has appropriate experience to be a member of an arbitral panel for the purposes of this Part.  (3) In listing a person on the register, the ACMA must consider requirements (if any) specified in regulations made for the purposes of this subsection. Subdivision B—Starting arbitration" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA must establish and keep a register of bargaining code arbitrators.  (2) Each such person listed on the register must be:  (a) a person experienced in legal matters, economic matters or industry matters; or  (b) a person who the ACMA considers has appropriate experience to be a member of an arbitral panel for the purposes of this Part.  (3) In listing a person on the register, the ACMA must consider requirements (if any) specified in regulations made for the purposes of this subsection. Subdivision B—Starting arbitration"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ae540505e0add9735b3089974848fe41e03677b18f16dc07c8ec1737260d03fe" ;
    cof:pageNumber "477"^^xsd:integer ;
