doc:sec-52zx-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "52ZX(4) Final offer arbitration" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A final offer:  (a) cannot be submitted later than the latest of the following:  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4 News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA Arbitration about remuneration issue  Division 7  Section 52ZX  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (i) the end of the period of 10 business days after the day on which the arbitration starts;  (ii) if a bargaining party makes a request under subsection 52ZT(1) (information requests)—the end of the period of 10 business days after the latest day on which the other bargaining party may comply with the request in accordance with subsection 52ZT(5);  (iii) if a bargaining party makes an application under subsection 52ZU(1) (challenges to information requests)—the end of the period of 10 business days after the day on which the panel makes a ruling in relation to the application under subsection 52ZU(3);  (iv) if regulations made for the purposes of this subparagraph specify a different period—the end of that period;  (v) if the panel considers that exceptional circumstances justify a different period—the end of that period; and  (b) cannot be more than 30 pages in length." ;
    cof:pageNumber "486"^^xsd:integer .

