doc:sec-52zx-ss-9 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "52ZX(9) Final offer arbitration" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(9) If one bargaining party fails to submit to the panel a final offer for what the remuneration amount should be, in accordance with subsection (4), the panel must:  Chapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc. Part IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code" ;
    cof:pageNumber "486"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zy a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "52ZY Final offer arbitration—termination of arbitration if no final"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-52zy ;
    values:originalText "offers  If both bargaining parties fail to submit to the panel a final offer for what the remuneration amount should be, the arbitration terminates on the day after the last day on which such a final offer could have been submitted in accordance with subsection 52ZX(4).  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4 News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA Arbitration about remuneration issue  Division 7  Section 52ZZ  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  52ZZ  Matters to consider in arbitration, etc.  (1) In making a determination under subsection 52ZX(1) (including in complying with subsections 52ZX(7), (8) and (9)), the panel must consider the following matters:  (a) the benefit (whether monetary or otherwise) of the registered news business’ covered news content to the designated digital platform service;  (b) the benefit (whether monetary or otherwise) to the registered news business of the designated digital platform service making available the registered news business’ covered news content;  (c) the reasonable cost to the registered news business of producing covered news content;  (ca) the reasonable cost to the designated digital platform service of making available covered news content in Australia;  (d) whether a particular remuneration amount would place an undue burden on the commercial interests of the designated digital platform service.  (2) In considering the matters set out in subsection (1), the panel must consider the bargaining power imbalance between Australian news businesses and the designated digital platform corporation. 52ZZA  Other requirements for arbitration determination  (1) The panel must make the determination no later than 35 business days (or, if the regulations specify a different period, the end of that period) after the latest of the following days:  (a) the last day on which a final offer may be submitted in accordance with subsection 52ZX(4);  (b) the last day on which a submission may be given by a bargaining party in accordance with subsection 52ZZB(1);  (c) the last day on which a submission may be given by the Commission in accordance with subsection 52ZZC(1);  (d) the last day on which a submission may be given by a bargaining party in accordance with subsection 52ZZC(3).  Chapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc. Part IVBA  News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code" ;
    skos:definition "offers  If both bargaining parties fail to submit to the panel a final offer for what the remuneration amount should be, the arbitration terminates on the day after the last day on which such a final offer could have been submitted in accordance with subsection 52ZX(4).  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4 News media and digital platforms mandatory bargaining code  Part IVBA Arbitration about remuneration issue  Division 7  Section 52ZZ  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  52ZZ  Matters to consider in arbitration, etc.  (1) In making a determination under subsection 52ZX(1) (including in complying with subsections 52ZX(7), (8) and (9)), the panel must consider the following matters:  (a) the benefit (whether monetary or otherwise) of the registered news business’ covered news content to the designated digital platform service;  (b) the benefit (whether monetary or otherwise) to the registered news business of the designated digital platform service making available the registered news business’ covered news content;  (c) the reasonable cost to the registered news business of producing covered news content;  (ca) the reasonable cost to the designated digital platform service of making available covered news content in Australia;  (d) whether a particular remuneration amount would place an undue burden on the commercial interests of the designated digital platform service.  (2) In considering the matters set out in subsection (1), the panel must consider the bargaining power imbalance between Australian news businesses and the designated digital platform corporation. 52ZZA  Other requirements for arbitration determination  (1) The panel must make the determination no later than 35 business days (or, if the regulations specify a different period, the end of that period) after the latest of the following days:  (a) the last day on which a final offer may be submitted in accordance with subsection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0813cd028dac9ca6ffd92a60b241cca154ec936b8abdcce3189aa6f7a2f53237" ;
    cof:pageNumber "488"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zy-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zy-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-52zy-ss-1 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
