    skos:definition "(2) A gas market instrument that provides for the charging of a fee may deal with any of the following matters:  (a) the amount of the fee, including a method for working out the amount of the fee;  (b) who is liable to pay the fee;  (c) the consequences of not paying the fee;  (d) when the fee becomes due and payable;  (e) waiving a fee;  (f) refunding a fee."@en ;
