doc:sec-53zn-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "53ZN(2) Proceedings for defamation not to lie" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) This section does not limit subsection 53J(2).  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc.  Chapter 4 Gas market  Part IVBB Compliance with gas market instruments  Division 3  Section 53ZO  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Subdivision D—Orders to redress loss or damage suffered by non-parties etc. 53ZO  Orders to redress loss or damage suffered by non-parties etc. Orders" ;
    cof:pageNumber "538"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "53ZN(1) Proceedings for defamation not to lie"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-53zn-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person engaged in conduct (the contravening conduct) that constituted a contravention or a related contravention of a civil penalty provision of a gas market instrument; and  (b) the contravening conduct caused, or is likely to cause, a class of persons to suffer loss or damage; and  (c) the class includes persons (non-parties) who are not, or have not been, parties to a proceeding (an enforcement proceeding) instituted under Part VI in relation to the contravening conduct; any court having jurisdiction in the matter may, on the application of the Commission, make such order or orders (other than an award of damages) as the court thinks appropriate against a person referred to in subsection (2). Note: The orders that the court may make include all or any of the orders set out in section 53ZP." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person engaged in conduct (the contravening conduct) that constituted a contravention or a related contravention of a civil penalty provision of a gas market instrument; and  (b) the contravening conduct caused, or is likely to cause, a class of persons to suffer loss or damage; and  (c) the class includes persons (non-parties) who are not, or have not been, parties to a proceeding (an enforcement proceeding) instituted under Part VI in relation to the contravening conduct; any court having jurisdiction in the matter may, on the application of the Commission, make such order or orders (other than an award of damages) as the court thinks appropriate against a person referred to in subsection (2). Note: The orders that the court may make include all or any of the orders set out in section 53ZP."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d5159ceefcde6c5eb68c39fa9440942a6c769cc4cc4975591d8cbd0f424c7470" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn ;
    cof:pageNumber "538"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may make orders against a person referred to in subsection (2) if the contravening conduct caused loss or damage to a class of persons. No defamation action against Commonwealth, Commission, or staff in relation to notice issuance." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.538" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-53zn-ss-1-norm .
