doc:sec-53zp a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "53ZP Kinds of orders that may be made to redress loss or damage" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "suffered by non-parties etc.  Without limiting subsection 53ZO(1), the orders that a court may make under that subsection against a person (the respondent) include all or any of the following:  (a) an order declaring the whole or any part of a contract made between the respondent and a non-party referred to in that subsection, or a collateral arrangement relating to such a contract:  (i) to be void; and  (ii) if the court thinks fit—to have been void ab initio or void at all times on and after such date as is specified in  Chapter 4  Provisions relating to particular industries, payment surcharges etc. Part IVBB  Gas market" ;
    cof:pageNumber "541"^^xsd:integer .

